<!--
    kuna `returndup auto`, the default: in an optimized function, adjacent
    guards whose arms print the same bare return fold into one guard joined by
    `||`, unless both tests call something and the return is void or a
    constant.

    Stage / sub-stage: P8 "goto-quality", a print-tree edit after final
    structuring (ActionRetShape, right before tailform).  The P0 assertion
    `option returndup record` keeps the guards as structuring left them.

    The image is decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/
    retshape_gcc_O2_x86_64, loaded whole.  `mutable_ptr` is
    `if (sane(b) != 0 || b->readonly || b->refcount > 1) return 0;`, which the
    split shared return prints as three guards; `settle` checks two calls'
    results with one `return;` each, as the source does.

    Pass 1 runs with the default: one `||` guard, and settle's two guards.
    Pass 2 (`option returndup record`) prints mutable_ptr's three guards.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/retshape_gcc_O2_x86_64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function mutable_ptr</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function settle</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option returndup record</com>
  <com>load function mutable_ptr</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
</script>
